---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro"
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro"
import PlatePanel from "../components/PlatePanel.astro"
import { requireClaim } from "../content/claims"
import { routes } from "../content/routes"
import study from "../content/2026-08-09-runtime-study.json"

const studyClaim = requireClaim("agent-runtime-study")
const discussionUrl = "https://x.com/kyashrathore/status/2082195455107268983"
const integer = new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US")
const percent = (value: number) => `${value.toFixed(2)}%`
const seconds = (value: number) => `${(value / 1000).toFixed(1)}s`
const command = "npx github:kyashrathore/agent-runtime-stats"
const title = "How often do coding agents need a full machine? — Claxedo"
const description = `Across ${integer.format(study.scope.executionCalls)} coding-agent execution calls, the median interval before a full machine was needed again was ${seconds(study.metrics.medianFullMachineReturnIntervalMs)}.`
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} image="/agent-runtime-study-og.png" canonicalPath={routes.agentRuntimeStudy}>
  <Nav />
    <main id="main-content" class="page">
      <article>
        <header class="study-hero">
          <div class="study-wrap hero-grid">
            <div class="hero-copy">
              <h1>How often do coding agents need a full machine?</h1>
              <p class="hero-lede">After an agent finished one full-machine call, it needed the machine again a median of {seconds(study.metrics.medianFullMachineReturnIntervalMs)} later.</p>
              <div class="hero-actions">
                <div class="hero-command"><code>{command}</code><button class="btn-primary" type="button" data-copy-command data-label="Copy">Copy</button></div>
                <a class="quiet-link" href={discussionUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Original discussion on X <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                <a class="quiet-link" href="https://github.com/kyashrathore/agent-runtime-stats" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Analyzer source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
              </div>
              <p class="meta">Claxedo research, 9 August 2026</p>
            </div>
            <PlatePanel plate="humayun" x={0.5} y={0.6} class="finding-panel"><aside class="card hero-finding" aria-label="Primary finding">
              <span class="finding-label">Median interval before the full machine was needed again</span>
              <span class="finding-prefix">Every</span>
              <strong>{seconds(study.metrics.medianFullMachineReturnIntervalMs)}</strong>
              <p>{integer.format(study.metrics.fullMachineReturnIntervalSamples)} measured intervals · p95 {seconds(study.metrics.p95FullMachineReturnIntervalMs)}</p>
            </aside></PlatePanel>
          </div>
        </header>

        <section class="study-section" aria-labelledby="finding-title">
          <div class="study-wrap section-head">
            <h2 id="finding-title">Your agent needs the machine again too soon to shut it down between calls.</h2>
            <p>The median gap between machine-required calls was {seconds(study.metrics.medianFullMachineReturnIntervalMs)}. Ninety-five percent of measured gaps were under {seconds(study.metrics.p95FullMachineReturnIntervalMs)}. Any system that releases the machine between calls has only that interval to provision another machine, synchronize changes, restore state, and become ready.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="study-section" aria-labelledby="break-even-title">
          <div class="study-wrap break-even-layout">
            <div class="section-head">
              <h2 id="break-even-title">Your handoff must be faster than the gap.</h2>
              <p>Let <code>y</code> be the time required to provision a machine, synchronize files, restore processes, and become ready. Let <code>x</code> be the time before the agent needs the machine again.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="equation-card">
              <span class="label">Required condition</span>
              <p><var>y</var> <b>&lt;</b> <var>x</var></p>
              <dl><div><dt>Median x</dt><dd>{seconds(study.metrics.medianFullMachineReturnIntervalMs)}</dd></div><div><dt>p95 x</dt><dd>{seconds(study.metrics.p95FullMachineReturnIntervalMs)}</dd></div></dl>
            </div>
            <div class="threshold-copy">
              <p>If <code>y ≥ {seconds(study.metrics.medianFullMachineReturnIntervalMs)}</code>, the machine will not be ready for at least half of the observed returns. Turning it off between calls would slow the agent instead of saving useful capacity.</p>
              <p>Even when <code>y &lt; {seconds(study.metrics.medianFullMachineReturnIntervalMs)}</code>, actual savings still depend on VM pricing, minimum charge periods, and idle-retention policy.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="study-section" aria-labelledby="prevalence-title">
          <div class="study-wrap">
            <div class="section-head">
              <h2 id="prevalence-title">Full-machine demand appears across most sessions and most turns.</h2>
              <p>Full-machine operations represented {percent(study.metrics.fullMachineExecutionCallPercent)} of execution calls, but appeared in {percent(study.metrics.turnsRequiringFullMachinePercent)} of resolved turns and {percent(100 - study.metrics.sessionsWithoutFullMachinePercent)} of classified sessions. Among turns that needed a full machine, {percent(study.metrics.repeatFullMachineTurnPercent)} called it again.</p>
            </div>
            <dl class="prevalence-grid">
              <div><dt>Classified sessions requiring a full machine</dt><dd>{percent(100 - study.metrics.sessionsWithoutFullMachinePercent)}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Resolved turns requiring a full machine</dt><dd>{percent(study.metrics.turnsRequiringFullMachinePercent)}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Full-machine turns calling it again</dt><dd>{percent(study.metrics.repeatFullMachineTurnPercent)}</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Execution calls requiring a full machine</dt><dd>{percent(study.metrics.fullMachineExecutionCallPercent)}</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="study-section" aria-labelledby="implication-title">
          <div class="study-wrap implication-layout">
            <div class="section-head">
              <h2 id="implication-title">A lightweight shell can reduce machine work. It cannot make the machine disappear.</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="body-copy">
              <p>A hybrid runtime helps when lightweight operations genuinely avoid a machine call. But the full machine remains part of the agent’s active execution path, and the measured return interval leaves very little time to discard and reconstruct it.</p>
              <p>Unless your complete handoff is comfortably below the observed interval, keeping a machine available during active work is simpler and faster than repeatedly rebuilding machine state.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="study-section" aria-labelledby="boundary-title">
          <div class="study-wrap">
            <div class="section-head">
              <h2 id="boundary-title">A call is machine-required when a lightweight virtual shell cannot faithfully execute it.</h2>
              <p>Calls supported by <a href="https://github.com/vercel-labs/just-bash" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vercel Labs’ just-bash ↗</a> remain classified as lightweight. Calls that cannot be classified honestly remain unresolved and are excluded from placement percentages.</p>
            </div>
            <ul class="boundary-list" aria-label="Full-machine call categories">
              <li><strong>Native executables</strong><p>System binaries outside the lightweight shell’s supported command set.</p></li>
              <li><strong>Package and development runners</strong><p>Builds, tests, and development servers that invoke a host runtime.</p></li>
              <li><strong>Git repository operations</strong><p>Commands that depend on native Git and the repository’s live state.</p></li>
              <li><strong>Browser testing</strong><p>Local browsers, automation processes, services, and their ports.</p></li>
              <li><strong>Interactive processes</strong><p>Commands requiring a TTY or a long-running process lifecycle.</p></li>
              <li><strong>Generated code execution</strong><p>Running agent-generated programs crosses the isolation boundary.</p></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="study-section" id="methodology" aria-labelledby="methodology-title">
          <div class="study-wrap methodology-layout">
            <div class="section-head">
              <h2 id="methodology-title">Local transcripts. Aggregate results.</h2>
              <p>The analyzer classified {integer.format(study.scope.executionCalls)} execution calls from {integer.format(study.scope.transcriptStores)} local transcript stores. It measured {integer.format(study.metrics.fullMachineReturnIntervalSamples)} intervals from the completion of one machine-required call to the start of the next within the same agent turn.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="method-cards">
              <article><span>Coverage</span><strong>{percent(study.metrics.turnCoveragePercent)}</strong><p>Execution-call turn coverage. Unresolved calls were reported separately rather than counted as lightweight or machine-required.</p></article>
              <article><span>Privacy</span><strong>Local first</strong><p>Raw transcripts, prompts, commands, paths, tool inputs, repository names, and user identifiers remain local.</p></article>
              <article><span>Measured</span><strong>Execution demand</strong><p>Observed runtime requirements and intervals between full-machine calls inside the same turn.</p></article>
              <article><span>Not measured</span><strong>Environment readiness</strong><p>Provisioning, synchronization, restoration time, VM pricing, and idle-retention cost require execution-platform telemetry.</p></article>
            </div>
            <p class="claim-note">Verified public claim: {studyClaim.publicWording}</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="run-section" id="run" aria-labelledby="run-title">
          <div class="study-wrap run-panel">
            <div class="section-head"><h2 id="run-title">How often does your agent need a full machine?</h2><p>Run the analyzer locally against supported coding-agent transcripts. See the complete report, then save a shareable page.</p></div>
            <div class="command-block"><span>Terminal</span><code>{command}</code><button class="btn-primary" type="button" data-copy-command data-label="Copy command">Copy command</button></div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </article>
    </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<script define:vars={{ command }}>
  document.querySelectorAll("[data-copy-command]").forEach((element) => {
    if (!(element instanceof HTMLButtonElement)) return
    element.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const label = element.dataset.label ?? "Copy command"
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(command)
        element.textContent = "Copied to clipboard"
      } catch {
        element.textContent = "Copy failed"
      }
      window.setTimeout(() => { element.textContent = label }, 1800)
    })
  })
</script>

<style>
  .study-wrap { width: var(--width); margin-inline: auto; }
  .study-hero { padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem) 0 0; }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, .85fr); gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem); align-items: center; }
  .hero-lede { max-width: 40rem; margin: 1.25rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-body); font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 1rem 1.5rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .hero-command { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .9rem; min-width: 0; padding: .35rem .35rem .35rem 1rem; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--surface); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--line); }
  .hero-command code { color: var(--ink); font-size: .8125rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  .hero-command button { flex: none; min-height: 2.25rem; padding: 0 1rem; font-size: .875rem; }
  .meta { margin: 1.5rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .875rem; }
  .study-hero :global(.finding-panel) { display: grid; place-items: center; padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem); }
  .hero-finding { display: grid; gap: .5rem; width: min(100%, 22rem); }
  .finding-label, .label { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .875rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  .finding-prefix { margin-top: .75rem; font: 400 1.75rem/1 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.025em; }
  .hero-finding strong { font: 400 clamp(4rem, 7vw, 6rem)/.9 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.05em; white-space: nowrap; }
  .hero-finding p { margin: .75rem 0 0; font-size: .875rem; }
  .study-section, .run-section { margin-top: var(--section); }
  .break-even-layout, .implication-layout, .methodology-layout, .run-panel { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem); align-items: start; }
  .equation-card { display: grid; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.75rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow-card); }
  .equation-card > p { margin: .5rem 0; font: 400 clamp(4rem, 7vw, 6rem)/.9 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.05em; }
  .equation-card var { font-style: normal; }
  .equation-card b { color: var(--ink-soft); font-weight: 400; }
  .equation-card dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; margin: 0; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .equation-card dt { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .875rem; }
  .equation-card dd { margin: .25rem 0 0; font: 400 1.5rem var(--font-display); }
  .threshold-copy { grid-column: 1 / -1; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .threshold-copy p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-body); line-height: 1.6; }
  code { color: var(--ink); font-size: .92em; }
  .prevalence-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 0; }
  .prevalence-grid div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; min-height: 12rem; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow-card); }
  .prevalence-grid dt { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .9375rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .prevalence-grid dd { margin: 0; font: 400 clamp(2.5rem, 4.5vw, 3.75rem)/1 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.04em; }
  .body-copy { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .body-copy p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-body); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .boundary-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .boundary-list li { min-height: 9rem; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow-card); }
  .boundary-list strong { display: block; font: 400 1.25rem/1.3 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.015em; }
  .boundary-list p { margin: .5rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .9375rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .section-head a { color: var(--ink); }
  .method-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .method-cards article { padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow-card); }
  .method-cards span { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .875rem; }
  .method-cards strong { display: block; margin: 1.25rem 0 .5rem; font: 400 1.5rem var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .method-cards p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .9375rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .claim-note { grid-column: 2; margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .875rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .run-panel { align-items: center; }
  .run-panel .section-head { margin: 0; }
  .command-block { display: grid; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--ink); color: var(--bg); }
  .command-block span { color: #a8a8a8; font-size: .875rem; }
  .command-block code { color: var(--bg); font-size: clamp(.8rem, 1.7vw, 1rem); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .command-block button { width: fit-content; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 60rem) {
    .hero-grid, .break-even-layout, .implication-layout, .methodology-layout, .run-panel { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .threshold-copy, .claim-note { grid-column: 1; }
    .prevalence-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .boundary-list { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .hero-actions { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
    .hero-command { border-radius: 16px; justify-content: space-between; }
    .hero-command code { min-width: 0; white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .threshold-copy, .prevalence-grid, .boundary-list, .method-cards { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
</style>
